From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 103] panvk: do not use DRM syncobj payload copy on kbase

Purpose: kbase devices do not expose DRM syncobjs.  Leave copy_sync_payloads
unset so VK_ANDROID_native_buffer release uses QueueSubmit2 followed by
GetSemaphoreFdKHR, which routes through the kbase sync_file exporter.

Observed failure before this patch:
  [ANB-SYNC] release path=copy_sync_payloads
  [ANB-SYNC] copy_sync_payloads result=-13
  QueueSignalReleaseImageANDROID failed: -13

Target: Mali-G615 MC6 / Poco X6 Pro / Kbase CSF v11
Mesa base: 5a07217f034b3e50d8c7c7794f97a2df1742613b

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c
index 17b3987..eef6e48 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c
@@ -494,7 +494,19 @@ panvk_per_arch(create_device)(struct panvk_physical_device *physical_device,
    device->vk.shader_ops = &panvk_per_arch(device_shader_ops);
    device->vk.check_status = panvk_device_check_status;
    device->vk.get_timestamp = panvk_device_get_timestamp;
+#ifdef HAVE_PAN_KMOD_KBASE
+   /* kbase does not expose DRM syncobjs.  Using the DRM payload-copy helper
+    * on a kbase logical device makes VK_ANDROID_native_buffer release fail
+    * before the submitted wait semaphore can be converted to a SYNC_FD.
+    * Leave this callback NULL so vk_common_QueueSignalReleaseImageANDROID()
+    * uses QueueSubmit2 and then exports the kbase sync via GetSemaphoreFdKHR.
+    */
+   device->vk.copy_sync_payloads = physical_device->kbase_node_path[0]
+                                      ? NULL
+                                      : vk_drm_syncobj_copy_payloads;
+#else
    device->vk.copy_sync_payloads = vk_drm_syncobj_copy_payloads;
+#endif
 
    device->kmod.allocator = (struct pan_kmod_allocator){
       .zalloc = panvk_kmod_zalloc,
